---
const points = [
  {
    title: "Spreadsheets and tickets",
    body: "Most contractors are onboarded through a help-desk ticket and offboarded through a forgotten one. There is no system of record.",
  },
  {
    title: "Access outlives the contract",
    body: "Without a controlled lifecycle, partner accounts stay active months past the engagement. Auditors find them before you do.",
  },
  {
    title: "Compliance evidence is manual",
    body: "Quarterly access reviews, certifications, and offboarding proofs are reconstructed from logs every audit cycle.",
  },
];
---
<section class="border-b border-paper-300 bg-paper-100">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-300 mb-4">The problem</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold max-w-3xl leading-tight">
      Identity governance was built for employees. The risk is everyone else.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-ink-500 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
      Contractors, partners, vendors, and guest users now outnumber employees in many
      enterprises. They have access to the same systems, but no HRIS owns their lifecycle.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-paper-300 border border-paper-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      {points.map((p) => (
        <div class="bg-paper-50 p-6">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">{p.title}</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 leading-relaxed">{p.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
